{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 12, :comments ["<b>My covenant of peace.</b> From the angel of death, in the sense of עֹשֶׂה שָׁלוֹם בִּמְרוֹמָיו (Job 25:2) — for indeed destruction occurs only on account of the opposition of contraries. And this was indeed fulfilled in Phinehas, who lived a very long time beyond all other men of his generation, so that he was serving in the Tabernacle at Shiloh in the time of the concubine at Gibeah (Judges 20:28), which was without question after the death of Joshua and the rest of the elders who outlived Joshua (Joshua 24:31). How much more so if this was in the time of Jephthah, who wrote to the king of the children of Ammon: בְּשֶׁבֶת בְּנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל בְּחֶשְׁבּוֹן וּבִבְנוֹתֶיהָ וגו׳ שְׁלֹשׁ מֵאוֹת שָׁנָה (Judges 11:26). And the Sages of blessed memory already recounted that Phinehas did not wish to go then to Jephthah to annul his vow. How much more so according to the one who says אֵלִיָּהוּ זֶה פִּינְחָס — and he is still alive and enduring."], :book :numbers, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 25, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:41:12.501381594Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}